# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12: a `sub:` returns nothing, so a `return` with a value in its body is
# refused -- in a block as at its top, in the words a named Structure's body gets.  It was "unsupported
# body".
sub: s ()
    int: n 0
    if: n = 0
        return: 5
    n: 1
end: s
s()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
